    "body": "A selected retained value could not condition another source read. This change learns a signed-H4 first-relation/operator choice, follows the selected value by exact owner identity, and copies from the final versioned record. Both relation IDs survive observed commitment and restore. It reuses the current relation store, H4 learner and copy operator; serving adds integer/table execution only.\n\nOn 48 authored OPEN cases, angular answers **40/48**, matched exact-code **32/48**, parent **20/48**. The intermediate-disabled arm gets 20/48. Both fits preserve 62/62 earlier responses and 24/24 earlier transfer; final angular also preserves 28/28 longer-context answers/writes and 5/5 persistent-session turns. All four first-edge pairs change the final source correctly. Four unchanged generated Rust functions compile and pass 12 semantic assertions. No broad language or frontier qualification is claimed; one place name, Bath, overlaps inherited fit data.\n\nThe eight remaining revision failures are retained with input snapshots: the unchanged writer misbinds some `Now … in …` statements and writes spurious question records. The next implementation repairs that writer while preserving this reader. The first attempt's overly permissive unreachable-target accounting is separately preserved and corrected. Related to #1139; its full handoff remains open, and #1140 remains subsequent.\n\nValidation: release CLI/probes; 126 existing native model tests pass; the corrected new version test passes a focused opt-level0 rerun after fixing its untrained fixture. Nine standard allocation tests pass. The artifact-dependent census was explicitly run locally and measures zero allocations for ingest/select/observe/copy; model loading is outside the measured section. Actual dependent commitments restore, reject changed IDs and decline mismatched observations. Formatting, native architecture policy and claim wording pass. Protected native CI [run 34043979602](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/actions/runs/34043979602) passed the normal profile at 4764f3ee: 127 native model, 3 context, 9 allocation and 20 CLI tests, with zero failures. The one artifact-dependent allocation test was ignored in CI and explicitly passed locally. Four compatibility acknowledgements are not audit/fuzz/WASM/Gate-C results.\n\nModel work: 93.658/120 seconds this cycle, cumulative 1607.670/1800 seconds, leaving 192.330. Local engineering remains within 1200 seconds. A necessary 64 MiB storage increment is recorded under the owner's standing authorization, preserving 128 MiB margin and all material. The record and compact evidence link exact sources/artifacts, full cost counters and commands. Warm timings have different emitted work and do not establish a whole-model speedup.\n\nProtected auto-merge is enabled; at final verification the PR is first in the merge queue, awaiting its merge-group checks.\n",
